r"""
CHAIN-003 - An unauthenticated outsider eavesdrops on Rocket.Chat support
            conversations, becomes a chosen customer, and has the workspace mail
            that customer's conversation to the attacker

Steps (each proven on its own in stage 11; this script runs them as one attack):
  1. VULN-076  stream-room-messages decides Livechat access against the room the
               client names in extraData, not the room it subscribes to, so one
               chat of the attacker's own opens every other Livechat room's live
               stream.
               -> live read of other customers' conversations, and with it the
                  identifiers those customers type to the agent.
  2. VULN-001  registerGuest resolves a returning customer by phone number
               before the caller's own token and returns the matched visitor
               document, token included.
               -> the chosen customer's visitor token, which is the only
                  credential the visitor-side routes ask for.
  3. VULN-051  livechat/transcript takes the recipient address from the request
               body and interpolates attachment descriptions into the mail
               unescaped.
               -> the customer's whole conversation delivered to an attacker
                  address from the workspace's own sender, carrying
                  attacker-written HTML.

Vulnerable code:
  targets/rocket.chat/apps/meteor/server/stream/streamBroadcast.ts and the
      Livechat allowRead rule for stream-room-messages (extraData.rid decides)
  targets/rocket.chat/packages/omni-core/src/visitor/create.ts:112 (the phone
      branch copies the matched visitor's token into the upsert)
  targets/rocket.chat/apps/meteor/server/lib/omnichannel/sendTranscript.ts:162-199
      (recipient from the caller; attachment description concatenated into HTML)

The chain
---------
Each step supplies the next step's precondition. The attacker begins with
nothing: no account, no token, no knowledge of the workspace's customers. The
stream confusion gives it a live feed of other people's support conversations,
which is where customers type their phone numbers and order numbers. A phone
number read off that feed is the key that the visitor-registration endpoint
converts into that customer's bearer token. The token then satisfies the
transcript route, which is willing to mail the conversation anywhere.

What a successful run proves
---------------------------
From an anonymous position: another customer's live messages on the attacker's
socket, that customer's visitor token obtained from a phone number seen in the
feed, a message posted into their conversation as them, and the full transcript
of their conversation delivered to the attacker's mailbox from the workspace's
own address with a working attacker-authored link inside it.

Dependencies: requests, websocket-client.
"""
